might bring something similar to you back to life.

499
00:29:10,820 --> 00:29:16,820
但能够准确重建你真实的内在么？
But is there a way to exactly re-create your inner self?

500
00:29:48,800 --> 00:29:51,090
我们的大脑呢？
from our brains?

501
00:31:26,910 --> 00:31:30,610
挽救你的神经连接体中的所有的信息，
all the information held in the connectome, Ken says,

502
00:31:30,720 --> 00:31:34,310
就是要把你的脑当做一台计算机。
is to treat the brain like a computer.

503
00:31:35,480 --> 00:31:37,640
那么这是一台已经死了的计算机，
So, this is a dead computer.

504
00:31:37,750 --> 00:31:39,410
它已经过时了，
It's way out of date.

505
00:31:39,520 --> 00:31:41,540
而且主板已经烧了，
It has a burned-out motherboard,

506
00:31:41,660 --> 00:31:44,750
这基本上的确是台无法修复
and there's really essentially nothing I can do

507
00:31:44,860 --> 00:31:46,750
的电脑了。
to repair this computer.

508
00:31:46,860 --> 00:31:50,580
我真的对这样的情况感到很伤心，因为就是这台电脑
And I'm really sad about that, because this particular computer

509
00:31:50,700 --> 00:31:53,490
储存着我所有的结婚照片和我的博士论文，
has all my wedding photographs, my PhD thesis,

510
00:31:53,600 --> 00:31:55,420
我可以就这么把它当做废物
and I'm going to just toss it

511
00:31:55,540 --> 00:31:57,930
扔掉，并永远的失去它了，
into the trash and lose it forever.

512
00:31:58,040 --> 00:32:00,030
但是，当然，这并不是事实，
But, of course, that's not true.

513
00:32:00,140 --> 00:32:01,830
那些信息储存在
Those pieces of information

514
00:32:01,940 --> 00:32:04,600
其中的硬盘里，
are stored digitally on this hard drive,

515
00:32:04,710 --> 00:32:09,270
我可以把里面的信息复制到另外一个硬盘中，
and I can copy that information onto another hard drive.

516
00:32:09,380 --> 00:32:14,170
现在我说的是神经科学已经
Now, what I'm saying is that neuroscience has told us

517
00:32:14,290 --> 00:32:16,840
告诉我们的：我们本质上是脑内
that we, in essence, are digital information

518
00:32:16,960 --> 00:32:20,610
突触连接中储存的数字信息。
stored in the synaptic connections within our brain.

519
00:32:20,730 --> 00:32:23,580
如果我们在死时保留下脑，
If we preserve that brain at our death,

520
00:32:23,700 --> 00:32:27,350
其中也存有使我们成为唯一的信息--
then that information that makes us unique --

521
00:32:27,470 --> 00:32:30,290
所有的记忆--还没有丢失的，
all of those memories -- they're not lost,

522
00:32:30,400 --> 00:32:32,890
我们就可能把它们取出，
and they can be potentially brought back

523
00:32:33,010 --> 00:32:36,400
就和通过储存到另一台电脑把数字信息
just the same way digital information can be brought back

524
00:32:36,510 --> 00:32:38,570
保存下来的方法一样。
by putting it in a new computer.

525
00:32:38,680 --> 00:32:43,500
软件是被写在硬件上的，
Software is physically written onto a hard drive.

526
00:32:43,620 --> 00:32:46,170
制作一个硬件精确的复件，
Make an exact copy of a drive,

527
00:32:46,290 --> 00:32:50,980
你就会得到其中储存的信息的复制。
and you have an exact copy of the information it contains.

528
00:32:51,090 --> 00:32:54,650
Ken认为你脑中所有的信息
Ken believes all the information in your brain

529
00:32:54,760 --> 00:32:56,620
也是可以复制和储存的。
can also be copied and stored.

530
00:32:56,730 --> 00:32:58,950
为了保存上万亿连接体的
All you have to do to preserve

531
00:32:59,070 --> 00:33:01,290
神经连接，你需要做的
the connectome's trillions of neural connections

532
00:33:01,400 --> 00:33:03,370
就是复制出大脑这个硬件...
is to copy the brain's hardware...

533
00:33:05,540 --> 00:33:07,290
...一次一片。
...one slice at a time.

534
00:33:07,410 --> 00:33:11,730
Ken的脑部扫描装配线就像这样：
Ken's brain-scanning assembly line would work like this.

535
00:33:11,850 --> 00:33:13,700
在死亡的时候，
At the moment of death,

536
00:33:13,810 --> 00:33:18,040
提取出脑，并保存在塑胶中，
the brain is extracted and preserved in plastic.

537
00:33:18,150 --> 00:33:22,310
然后使用加热的金刚钻刀把脑切成小片，
The brain is then chopped by a heated diamond knife

538
00:33:22,420 --> 00:33:28,920
大约20立方微米，比头发丝还小40000倍，
into 20-micron cubes 40,000 times thinner than a human hair.

539
00:33:29,030 --> 00:33:33,690
这些薄片再次被切片，比原先再薄1000倍，
These tiny slices are sliced again, 1,000 times thinner,

540
00:33:33,800 --> 00:33:37,290
然后使用离子射线扫描，
then scanned by ion beams.

541
00:33:37,400 --> 00:33:40,630
这个过程重复数百万次，
The process is repeated millions of times

542
00:33:40,740 --> 00:33:43,530
直到整个脑全部经过扫描并数据化。
until the entire brain is digitized.

543
00:33:43,640 --> 00:33:45,270
嗯？
Hmm? Hmm?

544
00:33:45,380 --> 00:33:48,340
这项技术现今已经存在，
It is technology that exists today.

545
00:33:48,450 --> 00:33:51,640
我们已经使用极端的分辨率
We mapped small bits of neural tissue

546
00:33:51,750 --> 00:33:54,610
绘制了一小块神经组织，
at this ultimate resolution already.

547
00:33:54,720 --> 00:33:56,740
这样的分辨率极高
The resolution is so high

548
00:33:56,860 --> 00:34:01,120
以至于我们不仅能看到神经元之间的联系--
that we cannot only see the connections between neurons --

549
00:34:01,230 --> 00:34:05,320
我们还能区分其连接强度和类型，
we can also determine their strength and type.

550
00:34:05,430 --> 00:34:09,290
一旦我们拥有了绘制一个人脑的能力，
Once we have the ability to map a human brain

551
00:34:09,400 --> 00:34:11,830
以及其中的神经联系如何
and once we have the knowledge

552
00:34:11,940 --> 00:34:15,000
产生一个人思维的知识，
of how that generates a human mind,

553
00:34:15,110 --> 00:34:21,770
我们就能在计算机中模拟出脑，
we will be able to simulate that brain in a computer substrate

554
00:34:21,880 --> 00:34:26,510
使死者在电脑模拟中
and bring that individual back to life

555
00:34:26,620 --> 00:34:29,610
复活。
inside of a computer simulation.

556
00:34:30,670 --> 00:34:33,500
绘制人类思维在今天
Mapping the human mind today

557
00:34:33,610 --> 00:34:37,390
还需要如阿波罗计划的规模的昂贵项目，
would require an enormously expensive Apollo-sized project.

558
00:34:37,510 --> 00:34:42,030
但随着技术的不断廉价，这种困境会改善的。
But as technology gets cheaper, that could change.

559
00:34:42,310 --> 00:34:46,330
虽然现在绘制整个人脑
So, whereas it's tens of billions of dollars today

560
00:34:46,440 --> 00:34:48,170
需要数百亿美元，
to map a whole human mind,

561
00:34:48,360 --> 00:34:52,750
但一百年后，也许只需要几千美元，
it will be thousands of dollars 100 years from now.

562
00:34:52,870 --> 00:34:57,660
任何一个想要使用100年之后的
Anybody that wants to get to that future technology

563
00:34:57,770 --> 00:35:01,530
未来技术的人只需要把自己的脑保存起来。
just 100 years from now can get their brain preserved.

564
00:35:01,640 --> 00:35:06,700
想象下未来，在某个医院中
Imagine the future in which every hospital is equipped

565
00:35:06,820 --> 00:35:09,840
存放着你濒临死亡的脑，
to preserve your brain if you dip near death.

566
00:35:09,950 --> 00:35:14,110
上千个脑被切片、扫描，
Thousands of brains, sliced and scanned,

567
00:35:14,220 --> 00:35:18,550
准备成为曾经是死者新人口。
will be ready to form a new population of the formerly dead.

568
00:35:18,660 --> 00:35:20,980
那个人的脑
That person's brain

569
00:35:21,100 --> 00:35:23,450
放置在这架子上至少100年，
that's sitting there on the shelf for the last 100 years

570
00:35:23,570 --> 00:35:27,260
才能被取走、切片、成像、
can be taken off, sliced, imaged,

571
00:35:27,370 --> 00:35:30,660
下载到一个计算机模拟中。
and downloaded into a computer simulation.

572
00:35:30,770 --> 00:35:35,980
那个人复活后就像刚从一个长觉中醒来，
And that person wakes up like they were in a long sleep.

573
00:35:37,740 --> 00:35:44,170
我们作为自己的数字复制品活着，然后呢？
And if we live on as digital copies of ourselves, what then?

574
00:35:44,290 --> 00:35:47,640
生活就像是一个电脑程序么？
What would life be like as a computer program?

575
00:35:47,760 --> 00:35:50,280
我们如何互相交流？
How would we relate to each other?

576
00:35:50,390 --> 00:35:54,490
我们能忍受失去生理感受的生活么？
Could we bear to live without physical sensation?

577
00:35:56,300 --> 00:35:57,690
复活一个人脑，
To bring back a brain

578
00:35:57,800 --> 00:36:00,190
只需要把它丢入计算机中，
and just leave it in some computer

579
00:36:00,300 --> 00:36:03,230
没有腿脚，没有眼睛--
without legs, without arms, without eyes --

580
00:36:03,340 --> 00:36:07,700
当然，这种感受比死亡还要糟糕。
of course, that would be an experience worse than death.

581
00:36:07,810 --> 00:36:11,500
复活人类思维这些可能还不够，
Resurrecting the mind may not be enough.

582
00:36:11,610 --> 00:36:15,070
为了真实地活着，我们期望的是看到周围的世界，
To truly live again, we will want to see the world around us

583
00:36:15,180 --> 00:36:16,940
并碰触到我们所爱的人。
and touch the ones we love.

584
00:36:17,050 --> 00:36:20,640
而把重建的思维转移到生物躯体内
The challenges of restoring a mind to a biological body

585
00:36:20,760 --> 00:36:22,780
似乎还是不可逾越的。
seem insurmountable.

586
00:36:22,890 --> 00:36:26,050
但是还有另一个选择，
But there is another option.

587
00:36:26,160 --> 00:36:28,520
也许我们能够制造新躯体，
Perhaps we could build new bodies

588
00:36:28,630 --> 00:36:31,420
来容纳我们复活的思维--
to carry our resurrected minds --

589
00:36:31,530 --> 00:36:35,840
机械身体，就像这些。
robot bodies, like these.

590
00:36:38,680 --> 00:36:42,700
有一天，也许能够保留我们的思维，
Someday, we may be able to preserve our minds,

591
00:36:43,670 --> 00:36:46,460
但如果我们没有身体，
but our resurrection will be incomplete

592
00:36:46,570 --> 00:36:47,790
复活就不算完全--
if we don't have bodies --

593
00:36:47,900 --> 00:36:50,490
不是这些脆弱的充斥化学反应的皮囊，
not these fragile bags of chemicals,

594
00:36:50,610 --> 00:36:53,930
而是永远不会老化的完美的身体复制品，
but perfect replicas of ourselves that never age

595
00:36:54,180 --> 00:36:56,770
而且还能不断升级--
and can be constantly upgraded --

596
00:36:56,980 --> 00:37:01,840
携带我们数字思维的机器人身体。
robot vessels to carry our digitized minds.

597
00:37:01,950 --> 00:37:03,950
想象一下吧。
Think of it.

598
00:37:15,130 --> 00:37:19,790
在日本，机器人是日常生活的一部分，
In Japan, robots are a part of daily life.

599
00:37:19,910 --> 00:37:21,490
大多数机器人在工厂工作，
Most of them work in factories

600
00:37:21,610 --> 00:37:25,230
和它们制造的机器看起来并没太大差别，
and don't look too different from the machines they build.

601
00:37:25,440 --> 00:37:29,430
日本在机器人制造水平上领先世界，
But Japan also leads the world in building androids

602
00:37:29,540 --> 00:37:33,840
并跨越了机器和人类的界线。
that straddle the line between humans and machines.

603
00:37:35,980 --> 00:37:39,800
如果采用石黑浩的方法，未来的世界
If Hiroshi Ishiguro has his way, the world of the future

604
00:37:39,920 --> 00:37:42,970
将会充满如此真实的复制品，
will be filled with replicants so realistic,

605
00:37:43,090 --> 00:37:47,320
你无法将其与有血有肉的真实人类区分开。
you can't tell them apart from flesh-and-blood people.

606
00:37:49,090 --> 00:37:52,320
我的目的不仅仅是机器人，
My goal is not just about the android or robot, but you know,

607
00:37:53,090 --> 00:37:58,320
我感兴趣的是人类本身。
I am interested in the human self.

608
00:38:01,090 --> 00:38:03,320
我的目的是理解什么才是人类。
My goal is to understand what is a human.

609
00:38:04,110 --> 00:38:10,030
石黑研究室在测试机器人
Hiroshi's lab tests how much or how little humanity

610
00:38:10,150 --> 00:38:15,010
要到什么程度才能被人类接受。
androids need to be accepted by humans.

611
00:38:16,120 --> 00:38:19,180
他们已经生产出一系列的机器人，
They have produced a line of robots

612
00:38:19,290 --> 00:38:21,180
从与人类非常接近的
ranging from near human

613
00:38:21,290 --> 00:38:25,290
到那些让人印象深刻的生物。
to these almost impressionistic creatures.

614
00:38:26,290 --> 00:38:30,290
我一直在思考什么才是人机互动的重要因素？
What are the important factors for human-robot interactions?

615
00:38:31,500 --> 00:38:36,290
最后我决定开发最低限度的人类。
And then I decided to develop minimal humans.

616
00:38:40,240 --> 00:38:42,870
Elfoid机器人和人类特征具有
The Elfoid robots have a bare minimum

617
00:38:42,980 --> 00:38:44,370
最少的相似性，
of human characteristics,

618
00:38:44,480 --> 00:38:47,770
不过人们可以和它们互动。
yet people are able to relate to them.

619
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:52,280
未来，这也许是一种对于你的机器人躯体的
In the future, this might be the low-budget option

620
00:38:52,390 --> 00:38:54,180
低预算选择.
for your robot body.

621
00:38:54,290 --> 00:38:56,860
很简单，但功能齐全。
It's simple, but it does the job.

622
00:38:57,360 --> 00:38:58,660
非常感谢！
どうもありがとう！

623
00:38:58,760 --> 00:39:02,690
现在，Elfoid机器人是通过遥控器控制的，
For now, the Elfoid is remote-controlled,

624
00:39:02,800 --> 00:39:05,360
和黑石所有的机器人一样。
like all of Hiroshi's robots.

625
00:39:05,470 --> 00:39:09,260
软件能够分析操作者的面部表情，
Software reads the facial expressions of the operator

626
00:39:09,370 --> 00:39:12,160
并将表情信息传入机器人
and transmits them to tiny actuators

627
00:39:12,280 --> 00:39:15,270
人造皮肤下的致动器，
under the android's synthetic skin.

628
00:39:15,380 --> 00:39:19,580
这就可以模仿人类面部肌肉、
These mimic human facial muscles.

629
00:39:27,620 --> 00:39:31,750
而另一边则是Geminoids,
At the other end of the ladder are the Geminoids,

630
00:39:31,860 --> 00:39:34,950
意思是尽可能地模仿人类。
meant to mirror humans as closely as possible.

631
00:39:35,060 --> 00:39:39,260
Geminoids是真实人类的复制，
The Geminoids are replicas of real people.

632
00:39:39,370 --> 00:39:42,590
想象一个这样的身体，
Imagine a body like this

633
00:39:42,710 --> 00:39:46,860
装载着你的数字思维，
loaded with the contents of your digitized mind,

634
00:39:46,980 --> 00:39:49,230
或是你的意识，
or perhaps your disembodied consciousness

635
00:39:49,350 --> 00:39:51,840
通过一台大型计算机操纵，
would operate the android from a mainframe,

636
00:39:51,950 --> 00:39:56,370
就像从远距离控制这些机器人一样。
just as these robots are controlled from a distance.

637
00:39:56,490 --> 00:40:00,080
黑石已经在研究这项联系
Hiroshi is already working on the technology

638
00:40:00,190 --> 00:40:05,350
我们思维到机器人的这项技术了。
to connect our minds to the androids.

639
00:40:05,460 --> 00:40:06,890
如果可能的话...
If possible...

640
00:40:07,460 --> 00:40:10,700
我们希望能够将操作者的脑与机器人直接相连，
We want to connect the operator's brain to the android directly.

641
00:40:10,890 --> 00:40:12,890
算是一种“人/机”接口。
It's a brain/machine interface.

642
00:40:13,400 --> 00:40:15,890
我们现在正在研究这个。
So now we are studying about that.

643
00:40:17,140 --> 00:40:21,330
如果黑石能够完美地创造出人机接口，
If Hiroshi does perfect a brain/machine interface,

644
00:40:21,440 --> 00:40:24,870
他会亲自进行第一个测试--
he will probably first test it on himself --

645
00:40:24,980 --> 00:40:29,670
或者更准确得说，是他的复制品。
or, more precisely, his replicant.

646
00:40:29,790 --> 00:40:32,010
好的好的，他正在重启--重启。
Yeah, yeah. He's restarting -- restarting.

647
00:40:32,120 --> 00:40:33,210
好了。
Okay.

648
00:40:33,320 --> 00:40:35,220
是的，我们来了--我们现在回来了。
Yeah, we have come -- we have come back now.

649
00:40:36,990 --> 00:40:37,990
好的。
Okay.

650
00:40:38,100 --> 00:40:39,920
现在好了，你能看着我么？
Now it's okay. Can you look at me?

651
00:40:40,030 --> 00:40:41,820
-嗯。 -好的。
-Mm-hmm. -All right.

652
00:40:41,930 --> 00:40:44,850
黑石经常送一些代表他自身的
Hiroshi often sends his doppelganger to other countries

653
00:40:44,970 --> 00:40:46,290
幽灵到别的国家，
to represent him

654
00:40:46,400 --> 00:40:51,030
或是不能亲自授课时就用复制品代替。
or to teach classes that he's too busy to attend in the flesh.

655
00:40:51,140 --> 00:40:53,430
那么人们对我是什么反应呢？
How do people respond to this and me?

656
00:40:53,540 --> 00:40:55,300
也许他们--
Well -- well, maybe they were --

657
00:40:55,410 --> 00:40:58,200
刚接触时有些焦虑紧张，
in the first contact, they were a little bit nervous,

658
00:40:58,310 --> 00:40:59,440
不过一旦--
but, you know, once --

659
00:40:59,550 --> 00:41:01,770
一旦你开始讲话，
as you know that, once you start to talk,

660
00:41:01,880 --> 00:41:05,350
他们就可以集中于交谈上。
they can concentrate on the -- in a conversation.

661
00:41:07,320 --> 00:41:12,620
黑石基本上创造了他自己的机器人版本，
Hiroshi has essentially created a robot version of himself,

662
00:41:12,730 --> 00:41:15,350
而且它的硬件越好，
and the better his hardware gets,

663
00:41:15,460 --> 00:41:18,870
就越会被人们当做真人。
the more his androids pass for real people.

664
00:41:18,960 --> 00:41:21,870
很多情况已经发生了，这要取决于环境，
Already it happens. It depends on the situation.

665
00:41:21,880 --> 00:41:25,840
人们无法区分出哪个是哪个。
People cannot define which is which.

666
00:41:25,840 --> 00:41:28,970
“F”Geminoid 是个如此逼真的机器人，
The Geminoid "F" is an android so lifelike,

667
00:41:29,080 --> 00:41:31,630
它已经在舞台上参加表演，
it has performed onstage in plays,

668
00:41:31,750 --> 00:41:34,920
但它的发明者从不满足。
but its inventor is never satisfied.

669
00:41:35,150 --> 00:41:37,920
这还不够，我们能更加完善。
That is not enough.We can improve more.

670
00:41:38,150 --> 00:41:41,900
比如我们还能赋予其更像人类的面部表情，
For example we can give more human-like facial expressions

671
00:41:41,900 --> 00:41:44,920
如果我们想，就可以做得到。
and if we want, we can make it work.

672
00:41:45,890 --> 00:41:49,120
感谢您回答我的问题，教授。
Thank you for answering my questions, Professor.

673
00:41:49,230 --> 00:41:50,650
不客气。
You're welcome.

674
00:41:50,770 --> 00:41:54,020
这会是未来死者复活后的面貌--
This could be the future face of the living dead --

675
00:41:54,140 --> 00:41:57,960
尸体不会腐烂，而是光滑的硅质肉体--
not decaying corpses, but smooth silicon flesh --

676
00:41:58,070 --> 00:42:03,240
携带着我们曾经失去的爱人的思维的机器人。
robots carrying the minds of our long-lost loved ones.

677
00:42:03,370 --> 00:42:06,840
有一天可能我们全身都会被机器人替代，
Someday we will replace the whole body with a machine.

678
00:42:07,370 --> 00:42:10,840
然后我们会发现什么才是存留的人类部分。
Then we will see what is the last part of the human.

679
00:42:16,650 --> 00:42:23,520
永远不会说永别的日子也许很快就到了。
The day when we never have to say goodbye may soon be at hand.

680
00:42:23,630 --> 00:42:27,620
但你重新看到你死去的奶奶
But what would it be like to see your dead grandmother again,

681
00:42:27,730 --> 00:42:31,020
活在合成的身体内又会是什么样呢？
living inside a synthetic body?

682
00:42:31,140 --> 00:42:35,260
那么她还是你所认识的那个女人么？
Would she still be the woman you knew?

683
00:42:35,370 --> 00:42:38,030
直到这些都成现实我们才会知道。
We won't know until it happens.

684
00:42:38,140 --> 00:42:40,530
人类也许在某天
The human race may one day be filled

685
00:42:40,650 --> 00:42:43,770
会变成新的陌生的种族群体。
with new and unfamiliar ethnic groups.

686
00:42:43,880 --> 00:42:47,740
人类的下一步也许是机器人亡灵，
The people next door might be the robotic undead,

687
00:42:47,850 --> 00:42:50,510
社会最大的划分可能是
and the great divide in society

688
00:42:50,620 --> 00:42:54,780
那些只活过一次的人
would be between those who have lived only once

689
00:42:54,890 --> 00:42:59,220
和那些存活在他们第二个或第五个躯体中的人。
and those who are on their second or fifth body.

